From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 03:36:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: scaler: fill alpha for every RGB
 destination

The job word at 0x8c turns on a constant opaque alpha fill. It was set
only for an ARGB destination whose source has no alpha, so a Y'CbCr ->
XRGB job ran with the fill off. On the J604 (T8132) every such job
stayed running until the 500 ms watchdog reset the engine ("job timed
out (running 0x1)", 20 of 20 jobs, cold and warm), while the same job
to ARGB, which differs from it only in this word, completed in about
3 ms. XRGB carries an unused byte where ARGB carries alpha, so filling
it is harmless.

Set the fill for every R'G'B' destination when the source has no
alpha.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/scaler/apple-scaler-hw.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/scaler/apple-scaler-hw.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/scaler/apple-scaler-hw.c
index ff6d775113..0ced89c15c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/scaler/apple-scaler-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/scaler/apple-scaler-hw.c
@@ -415,8 +415,13 @@ int asc_job_build(const struct asc_job *job, struct asc_reg *w, unsigned int max
 	asc_emit_image(&e, &asc_rdma, &job->src);
 	asc_emit_image(&e, &asc_wdma, &job->dst);
 	asc_emit_memory(&e, job);
-	/* Alpha fill: constant opaque alpha when the source has none. */
-	asc_emit(&e, 0x8c, (d->alpha && !s->alpha ? BIT(31) : 0) | 0xffff);
+	/*
+	 * Alpha fill: constant opaque alpha when the source has none. Every
+	 * R'G'B' destination needs it, XRGB included: with the fill off and
+	 * no source alpha the engine never completes the job (the J604 timed
+	 * out on every Y'CbCr -> XRGB job while ARGB passed).
+	 */
+	asc_emit(&e, 0x8c, (!d->yuv && !s->alpha ? BIT(31) : 0) | 0xffff);
 	asc_emit_chroma(&e, job);
 	asc_emit_unscaled(&e, job);
 	if (job->csc)
